@startuml domain-access
' Report §2.4 — Access bounded context in full. The classes come from
' include/domain-access.iuml, the same source the overview (domain-model.puml) uses.
!pragma layout smetana
!include include/style.iuml
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

title Access context (ticketing-service) — domain model

!include include/domain-access.iuml
!include include/domain-published-language.iuml
!$only = "access"
!include include/domain-event-links.iuml

remove @unlinked
hide <<DomainEvent>> members

note top of Ticket
  <b>Invariants</b>
  · one ticket per confirmed session, not per registration
  · VOID: cannot be transferred or checked in
  · USED: cannot be transferred or checked in again
  · a TRANSFERRED ticket can be transferred again
  · transfer history is append-only
  · voidTicket() is a no-op on VOID or USED
end note

note bottom of CheckInPolicy
  Enforces two of the three rules in specs/3 §5.4:
  void tickets and duplicate check-ins. The third,
  "outside the session window", needs programme data
  this context does not hold (see specs/2 FR-13).
end note

legend right
  Value objects are Java records, mapped as JPA
  @Embeddable. CheckIn and TransferRecord are
  entities inside the Ticket aggregate (cascade ALL,
  orphanRemoval). checkedInAt - queuedAt is the
  gate wait that FR-16 will aggregate.
endlegend
@enduml
